<div class="wrap">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>Shipping &amp; returns</span>
  </nav>
</div>

<section class="wrap wrap-mid" style="padding-bottom:clamp(60px,8vw,110px)">
  <span class="eyebrow">Policies</span>
  <h1 style="margin:14px 0 18px">Shipping, returns &amp; payment</h1>
  <p class="lede">Plain answers, no small print games.</p>

  <div class="stack-32" style="margin-top:44px">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Shipping</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>Orders placed before 2:00pm on a business day are packed and dispatched the same day. Everything ships
          from our tea room in Canada with tracking.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">Standard</strong> — 2 to 5 business days domestically, 7 to 14 business days
          internationally. <%= money(store.flatShippingFee) %> flat, and complimentary on orders over
          <%= money(store.freeShippingThreshold) %>.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">Express</strong> — 1 to 2 business days, <%= money(store.flatShippingFee * 2) %>.</p>
        <p>Duties and import taxes on international orders are the customer's responsibility. Tea is a food product:
          some countries restrict the import of unprocessed leaf, and if a parcel is seized by customs we will refund
          the product cost.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Returns</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>Unopened, sealed tins can be returned within 30 days of delivery for a full refund of the product cost.
          Email us first and we will send a prepaid label for domestic orders.</p>
        <p>If you have opened a tea and it is not to your taste, tell us. We will replace it or refund it — this
          happens rarely, and it is a better outcome for both of us than an argument. We do not ask you to ship a
          half-used tin back across a border.</p>
        <p>Refunds are issued to the original card through OTT Pay and normally appear within 5 to 10 business days,
          depending on your bank.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Payment</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>We accept Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Discover, JCB, Diners Club and China UnionPay credit and
          debit cards. All payments are processed by <strong>OTT Pay</strong>, a PCI-DSS compliant payment provider,
          using a 3-D Secure 2 authenticated card-not-present transaction.</p>
        <p>3-D Secure 2 means your bank may ask you to confirm the payment — usually a code in your banking app, a
          text message, or a fingerprint. This is a security feature of the card scheme, not something we control,
          and it protects you against fraudulent use of your card.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">We never see or store your card number.</strong> The card details you type are
          transmitted directly to OTT Pay over TLS. Our database records only the card brand, the last four digits
          and the gateway's payment identifier so that we can reconcile an order or issue a refund.</p>
        <p>All prices are in <%= store.currency %> and include <%= store.taxLabel %> where applicable, calculated at
          checkout before you pay.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">3-D Secure and fraud</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>Every card payment on this site is screened in real time for fraud risk before authorisation. If a
          transaction is flagged we may contact you to confirm the order before shipping. A declined payment means
          your card was not charged — an authorisation that is later reversed will show a pending amount on your
          statement which your bank releases on its own schedule.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row" style="gap:12px;margin-top:40px;flex-wrap:wrap">
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/terms">Full terms &amp; privacy</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/order">Track an order</a>
    <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/shop">Shop the tea</a>
  </div>
</section>
